The canon follow-ups commit is done and in review with Sol and DeepSeek. It fixes four stale or overstated canon lines:
- the `sats-capped-run` path;
- the owner-routing paragraph, which now reads as a contract with a "not installed yet" status line;
- the worktree-cleanup claim, now scoped to F-D;
- the stale Muse PASTE-4 pointer.

It lands right after it passes.

One question came out of it. The routing change already on main says the T3 Code Nightly Upstream PRs lane stays open after it finishes, as a standing contribution lane. The producer found no decision of yours behind that line. The closest lead is a 14:06 Sats steer calling the lane "the permanent home for upstream PRs", which doesn't mention settling. If it's your rule, name the source and I'll add one cited sentence. If not, it should come out.

